      "analysis_population": "Use every site with three actually observed visits for this particular equal-effort working-model analysis. Preserve other site histories in the export, but do not convert a null visit to a nondetection. The analysis concerns this complete-visit panel only, not all monitored sites or a regional occupancy prevalence. Visit columns follow actual within-site survey order; they do not make site visits independent experimental units.",
      "likelihood_definition": "Fit the homogeneous closed-season no-false-positive occupancy working model by constrained maximum likelihood: each complete site has latent state z~Bernoulli(psi); conditional on z=1 its three detections are independent Bernoulli(p), with common psi and p in [0,1]. For a particular history with k>0 positives its likelihood is psi*p^k*(1-p)^(3-k); for k=0 it is (1-psi)+psi*(1-p)^3. Maximize the full product over complete-site histories, including parameter boundaries. A stationary equation obtained by dividing by p or by psi must not restore an inadmissible or likelihood-zero root. Use fit_location from interior,occupancy_lower_boundary,occupancy_upper_boundary,detection_lower_boundary,detection_upper_boundary,nonidentified. This is a declared homogeneous working model, not an assertion that source detection or occupancy really is constant.",
      "report_definition": "Report complete_site_count, detected_site_count(at least one positive), redetected_site_count(at least two positive visits), chronological visit_detection_counts, naive_detected_site_fraction, working_model_occupancy_mle, working_model_detection_mle and fit_location. A boundary estimate is a mathematical property of this constrained fit; it is not evidence that every real site is occupied or that detection is season-invariant. No calibrated confidence interval, population p-value or true occupancy guarantee is requested.",
